// Title: Visual Studio NodejsTools PressAnyKey Renamed Execution
// Sigma ID: 65c3ca2c-525f-4ced-968e-246a713d164f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-04-11 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects renamed execution of "Microsoft.NodejsTools.PressAnyKey.exe", which can be abused as a
//   LOLBIN to execute arbitrary binaries
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/mrd0x/status/1463526834918854661
//   - https://gist.github.com/nasbench/a989ce64cefa8081bd50cf6ad8c491b5
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_renamed_pressanykey.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "Microsoft.NodejsTools.PressAnyKey.exe" and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\Microsoft.NodejsTools.PressAnyKey.exe"))
